description:
**Responsibilities**
**RESPONSIBILITIES**

* Assisting Senior Technician in technical analysis;
* Analyse ground data and prepare base maps;
* Prepare graphic representations of a parcel of land or a portion of road (plan, profile and section);
* Annotate work to be done (barrier, border, pavement marking, etc.);
* Preparation of a highway, roadway and detour path;
* Plans and profiles, cross sections, typical sections and details
* Temporary or permanent signage design;
* Preparation of an installation slip;
* Other duties as assigned.

Key Competencies / Skills



* The successful candidate is likely to be having 5-15 years’ of highway work experience with consultancy firm or developer, International experience or Global design centre are an asset.
* Must have strong abilities to work with CAD, Microstation and Microsoft Office; Knowledge of InRoads, Openroads, Infraworks and Civil3D will be an asset.
* Ability to work on multiple projects at given time.
* Understanding of Canadian standards and design practices are an asset

**Desired Skills**

* Ability to work under pressure and with minimum of supervision
* Strong organization skills;
* Good written and spoken communication skills and be fluent in English
* Committed team player;
* Cultural awareness

**Qualifications**

* Diploma in Civil;
* 3-10 years’ working experience on infrastructure projects and detail design of highways and drainage.
* Experience to work in/with other cultures.
* English spoken and written
* French spoken and written a plus

Desirable Skills



* Professional licencing within Canada is an asset;
* Solid understanding of other road design requirements (e.g. drainage / hydraulic design, environmental design / mitigation measure, engineering surveys, geotechnical investigations and design);
* Solid understanding of Ministry of Transportation, Canadian standards and design practices are an asset;
* Familiarity with Canadian regulatory environment and experience with approval processes is an asset.

BGV:



* Employment with WSP India is subject to the successful completion of a background verification (“BGV”) check conducted by a third-party agency appointed by WSP India.
* Candidates are advised to ensure that all information provided during the recruitment process — including documents uploaded — is accurate and complete, both to WSP India and its BGV partner”.

